---
const clients = [
  { id: "a", name: "Client A" },
  { id: "b", name: "Client B" },
  { id: "c", name: "Client C" },
];
---

<section id="rt-demo" class="demo" aria-labelledby="rt-demo-title">
  <div class="demo-head" data-reveal="rise">
    <h2 id="rt-demo-title">SharedRichText, live</h2>
    <p>
      Three <code>watershed</code> documents share one
      rich-text channel over the <code>rich_text_kernel</code>. It runs the
      single-op-in-flight client-transform protocol from the{" "}
      <a href="/json-ot">json_ot demo</a> with the quill-delta algebra.
      Operations <em>retain</em>, <em>insert</em>, or <em>delete</em> text spans.
      An operation can also change attributes such as bold or color, or insert
      an image embed. Positions use UTF-16 code units, which Quill and
      JavaScript strings also use. Each editor keeps at most one operation in
      flight. Input received while that operation is pending combines into one
      buffered operation. SharedRichText uses OT. For CRDT plain text,{" "}
      <a href="/text"><code>SharedText</code></a> indexes graphemes by stable
      identity and converges by merge.
    </p>
    <p class="demo-hint">
      Local edits appear when you type. Type at the same position in two
      clients, apply different formatting to one span, or delete text while
      another client formats it. The operation log and canonical text show the
      convergence result. Dashed, colored peer cursors show each peer
      selection. The client transforms those selections through each edit.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="rig" data-rt-rig>
    {
      clients.map((c) => (
        <article
          class="client"
          data-client={c.id}
          aria-label={`${c.name} editor`}
          style={`grid-area: ${c.id}`}
        >
          <header class="client-head">
            <h3>{c.name}</h3>
            <span class="pending-count annot" data-pending-count>
              synchronized
            </span>
          </header>
          <div class="quill-mount" data-quill-root />
          <footer class="client-foot">
            <p class="canonical annot" data-canonical />
            <ul
              class="peer-list"
              data-peer-list
              aria-label={`Peer selections visible to ${c.name}`}
            />
          </footer>
        </article>
      ))
    }

    <div class="channel" style="grid-area: seq">
      <div class="seq-node" data-seq-node>
        <span class="annot">Sequencer</span>
        <output class="seq-counter" data-seq-counter aria-label="Latest sequence number">
          SN&nbsp;0
        </output>
      </div>
      <ol
        class="op-log"
        data-op-log
        aria-live="polite"
        aria-label="Sequenced rich-text operations, newest first"
      >
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="flow-layer" data-flow-layer aria-hidden="true"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="demo-controls" data-reveal="rise">
    <label class="latency">
      <span class="annot">Link latency</span>
      <input
        type="range"
        min="100"
        max="2000"
        step="100"
        value="700"
        data-rt-latency
        disabled
      />
      <output data-rt-latency-out>700 ms</output>
    </label>
    <label class="pace">
      <span class="annot">Animation speed</span>
      <input
        type="range"
        min="0.25"
        max="2"
        step="0.25"
        value="0.5"
        data-rt-pace
        title="Changes animation speed only. It does not affect simulated ordering."
        disabled
      />
      <output data-rt-pace-out>0.5×</output>
    </label>
    <label class="field-notes-toggle">
      <input
        type="checkbox"
        data-rt-latency-variance
        title="Add random ±50 ms per hop; arrival order may change."
        disabled
      />
      <span class="annot">Jitter ±50&nbsp;ms</span>
    </label>
    <p class="status" data-rt-status role="status">
      <span class="stamp converged">Converged</span>
      replicas match · no pending operations
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="scenario-row" data-reveal="rise">
    <button type="button" class="scenario-btn" data-rt-race-type disabled>
      Type at the same position
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="scenario-btn" data-rt-race-format disabled>
      Apply bold and color to one span
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="scenario-btn" data-rt-race-delete disabled>
      Delete and format the same span
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="scenario-btn" data-rt-embed disabled>
      Insert an image
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="step-btn" data-rt-step disabled>
      Deliver one operation
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="step-btn" data-rt-settle disabled>
      Deliver all operations
    </button>
    <button
      type="button"
      class="reset-btn"
      data-rt-reset
      aria-label="Reset all three editors to the initial formatted content"
      disabled
    >
      Reset
    </button>
  </div>

  <p class="controls-hint">
    Each scenario button submits through the corresponding Quill editor. This
    is the same path as keyboard input. You can also type and use the toolbar in
    all three editors. Edit one editor while another editor has a pending
    operation.
  </p>

  <noscript>
    <p class="demo-noscript">
      Enable JavaScript for the live demo. The browser runs the compiled
      production client runtime, <code>rich_text_kernel</code>, in-memory
      <code>sluice</code>, and Quill editor. The rest of the page works without
      JavaScript.
    </p>
  </noscript>

  <p class="demo-noscript" data-rt-fallback hidden>
    The live demo could not start because the browser did not load the compiled
    production client runtime, in-memory <code>sluice</code>, and Quill editor.
    The rest of the page works without the demo.
  </p>
</section>

<script>
  try {
    const { initRichTextDemo } = await import("../scripts/rich-text-demo.ts");
    initRichTextDemo();
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("watershed rich-text demo failed to start", error);
    const note = document.querySelector("[data-rt-fallback]");
    if (note instanceof HTMLElement) note.hidden = false;
  }
</script>

<style>
  /* A third, locally-scoped accent alongside the site's magenta
     (--overprint) / blue (--waterline) pair, for a third client's peer
     cursor and swatch. Chosen in the same oklch family, and — like a USGS
     sheet's green contour ink — reads as "original ground truth" next to
     magenta's "unverified revision", keeping the peer-color trio legible
     without introducing an unrelated hue to the palette. */
  :root {
    --client-a: var(--overprint-deep);
    --client-b: var(--waterline);
    --client-c: oklch(42% 0.13 150);
  }

  .demo {
    padding: var(--space-section) var(--content-pad);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }

  .demo-head {
    max-width: 68rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-h2);
    font-weight: 620;
    font-stretch: 118%;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    line-height: 1.05;
  }

  .demo-head p {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .demo-hint {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  /* ── client / editor grid ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .rig {
    position: relative;
    max-width: 68rem;
    margin: var(--space-xl) auto 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-areas:
      "a seq b"
      "c c   c";
    grid-template-columns: 1fr minmax(11rem, 0.7fr) 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .rig .client[data-client="c"] {
    justify-self: center;
    width: min(100%, 26rem);
  }

  .client {
    border: 1px solid var(--ink);
    background: var(--bg);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .client-head {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }

  .client-head h3 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 650;
    font-stretch: 115%;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .pending-count {
    color: var(--muted);
    transition: color var(--dur-state) var(--ease-out-quart);
  }

  .pending-count.is-pending {
    color: var(--overprint-deep);
  }

  /* Quill mounts its own toolbar + editor as siblings inside this node. */
  .quill-mount {
    min-height: 8rem;
  }

  .quill-mount :global(.ql-toolbar.ql-snow) {
    border: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
  }

  .quill-mount :global(.ql-container.ql-snow) {
    border: none;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
  }

  .quill-mount :global(.ql-editor) {
    min-height: 7rem;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .quill-mount :global(.ql-editor.ql-blank::before) {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-style: normal;
  }

  /* Presence cursors: quill-cursors paints inline styles for color, so this
     just tightens the flag/caret to the site's mono/annotation language. */
  .quill-mount :global(.ql-cursor-name) {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
  }

  .client-foot {
    margin-top: auto;
    padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md) var(--space-md);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }

  .canonical {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  .peer-list {
    margin: var(--space-xs) 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-2xs) var(--space-sm);
  }

  .peer-list li {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.3rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .peer-list :global(.peer-swatch) {
    display: inline-block;
    width: 0.55rem;
    height: 0.55rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
  }

  /* ── channel / sequencer ──────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .channel {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    padding-top: clamp(var(--space-md), 6vw, 4.5rem);
  }

  .seq-node {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-2xs);
    padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-lg);
    border: 1px solid var(--ink);
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--bg);
  }

  .seq-counter {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .seq-counter.stamped {
    animation: stamp 380ms var(--ease-out-quart);
  }

  @keyframes stamp {
    0% {
      color: var(--overprint);
      transform: scale(1.12);
    }
    100% {
      color: var(--ink);
      transform: none;
    }
  }

  .op-log {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    width: 100%;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--muted);
    overflow: hidden;
    max-height: 13.5rem;
    mask-image: linear-gradient(black 55%, transparent 96%);
  }

  .op-log :global(li) {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0 0.4rem;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 0.12rem 0;
  }

  .op-log :global(.op-meta) {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .op-log :global(.op-path) {
    color: var(--waterline);
  }

  .op-log :global(.op-kind) {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .op-log :global(li:first-child .op-meta) {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .flow-layer {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
    z-index: var(--z-flow);
  }

  :global(.flow-dot) {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    width: 10px;
    height: 10px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--overprint);
  }

  :global(.flow-dot.sequenced) {
    background: var(--ink);
  }

  :global(.flow-dot-label) {
    position: absolute;
    left: 50%;
    bottom: calc(100% + 4px);
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    white-space: nowrap;
    font-size: 0.625rem;
    line-height: 1;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    padding: 2px 5px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    color: var(--bg);
    background: var(--overprint);
  }

  :global(.flow-dot.sequenced .flow-dot-label) {
    background: var(--ink);
  }

  /* ── controls ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .demo-controls {
    max-width: 68rem;
    margin: var(--space-xl) auto 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .latency,
  .pace {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .latency input,
  .pace input {
    accent-color: var(--overprint);
    width: clamp(8rem, 18vw, 14rem);
  }

  .latency output,
  .pace output {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    min-width: 5ch;
  }

  .field-notes-toggle {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .field-notes-toggle input {
    accent-color: var(--overprint);
    width: 1.05rem;
    height: 1.05rem;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .status {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--muted);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .status :global(.stamp) {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.09em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 0.2rem 0.55rem;
    border: 1.5px solid currentColor;
    transform: rotate(-2deg);
  }

  .status :global(.stamp.converged) {
    color: var(--waterline);
  }

  .status :global(.stamp.revising) {
    color: var(--overprint-deep);
  }

  /* ── scenario row ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .scenario-row {
    max-width: 68rem;
    margin: var(--space-lg) auto 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-md);
  }

  .scenario-btn,
  .step-btn {
    padding: 0.65rem 1.2rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--ink);
    background: var(--bg);
    font-weight: 600;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition:
      background var(--dur-feedback) var(--ease-out-quart),
      transform var(--dur-feedback) var(--ease-out-quart);
  }

  .step-btn {
    border-color: var(--hairline);
    color: var(--muted);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .scenario-btn:hover:enabled,
  .step-btn:hover:enabled {
    background: var(--overprint-faint);
  }

  .scenario-btn:active:enabled,
  .step-btn:active:enabled,
  .reset-btn:active:enabled {
    transform: scale(0.97);
  }

  .reset-btn {
    padding: 0.65rem 1.2rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--muted);
    font-weight: 400;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition:
      background var(--dur-feedback) var(--ease-out-quart),
      color var(--dur-feedback) var(--ease-out-quart),
      transform var(--dur-feedback) var(--ease-out-quart);
  }

  .reset-btn:hover:enabled {
    background: var(--surface);
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .scenario-btn:disabled,
  .step-btn:disabled,
  .reset-btn:disabled {
    opacity: 0.45;
    cursor: default;
  }

  .controls-hint {
    max-width: 68rem;
    margin: var(--space-sm) auto 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .demo-noscript {
    max-width: 68rem;
    margin: var(--space-lg) auto 0;
    color: var(--overprint-deep);
  }

  @media (max-width: 1080px) {
    .rig {
      grid-template-areas: "a" "seq" "b" "c";
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .rig .client[data-client="c"] {
      justify-self: stretch;
      width: auto;
    }

    .op-log {
      max-height: 5.7rem;
    }
  }

  @media (pointer: coarse) {
    .scenario-btn,
    .step-btn,
    .reset-btn {
      padding: 0.85rem 1.2rem;
    }
  }
</style>
